WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.157
A CTE has a simple structure.

00:00:02.157 --> 00:00:04.002
WITH gives the stage a name.

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:08.232
The query inside the parentheses defines the rows and columns of that stage.

00:00:08.232 --> 00:00:11.202
The final query can read the CTE by name.

00:00:11.202 --> 00:00:15.492
You can also define several CTEs separated by commas.

00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:18.147
The CTE is not a permanent table.

00:00:18.147 --> 00:00:19.952
It belongs to the statement.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:25.832
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:25.832 --> 00:00:32.717
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:39.239
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
